# Tests #326 Cut B — controlled retry and explicit real boundaries

Prepared 2026-10-25T21:06:11.122529+00:00. Rook Ashwhisker <EXECUTOR>.

Source base: f5919267e2696773f909f69575810c9cb5c3c1e2. Scope: Oracle #326 Cut B plus messaging_flow (fb4fdb82), first evidence for #327. Own worktree/target, two Cargo jobs, O1, debug assertions, explicit private memory custody. No operator input or login Keychain.

Mechanisms: private Worker::refresh_identity_due accepts a clock; production still uses Instant::now and 30 seconds stamped after the refresh. Controlled test drives the exact boundary, ordered held-message signing, delayed legitimate artifact projection, unchanged original observation and tamper refusal. Detector test processes ten completed unchanged Git snapshots and one changed snapshot. No time is used to infer silence.

Real identity-local, provenance hold/Git, app custody and messaging GUI boundary bodies are retained byte-for-byte; only annotations/call placement changed. scripts/night-test-boundaries.sh invokes exact ignored test names, never blanket --ignored. Original 20 MiB seal/replay/producer-latency assertion remains there. Default messaging invariant stays active and retains local delivery, pending evidence, ordered signatures and bounded batches. Duplicate remote helper execution is removed; its standalone test remains.

The live replay fixture uses channels plus a producer-completion filesystem notification instead of a 750ms sleep. #276 remains active/default: equal 512KiB streams replace three 4MiB backgrounds, with every original quota/page-count, unfinished-background, exact Screen, GUI ACK and completion assertion retained. The watched-floor block precedes tail assertions so the mutation names the quota failure.

